          .num_example
            %h6#counterexample_2 Counterexample
            %p Any topos that violates countable choice, of which there are plenty, must also violate internal PAx.
          .num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              An interesting example of a topos that has enough projectives and satisfies internal CoSHEP (at least, assuming the axiom of choice in
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+topos"} effective topos
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/realizability+topos"} realizability topos
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+completions"} exact completions
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "/nlab/show/realizability+topos#pax"} this remark
          %p
            For a Grothendieck topos example, the sheaves on the interval
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,1]
            with its usual topology give a topos in which the internal axiom of countable choice fails, hence internal PAx must also fail.
          %h2#in_categories_which_are_not_topoi In categories which are not topoi
          .num_example
            %h6#example_4 Example
            %p
              According to Peter Scholze in
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2020/03/pyknoticity_versus_cohesivenes.html#c057798"} this comment on the nCafé
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/condensed+sets"} condensed sets
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              satisfies the axiom of choice. The category of condensed sets do not form a topos, only an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitary+pretopos"} infinitary pretopos
            %p However, internal CoSHEP fails in condensed sets.
          %h2#further_properties Further properties
          %p
            Since
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            is (essentially regardless of foundations) an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+category"} exact category
            %a{:href => "projective+object#EnoughProjectives"} enough projectives
            then it must be the
            %em free
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+category"} exact category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi PSet
                    %mrow
                      %mi ex
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi lex
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSet_{ex/lex}
            generated by its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi PSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSet
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+objects"} projective objects
            %a{:href => "regular+and+exact+completions#TheExLexCompletion"} ex/lex completion
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi PSet
                      %mrow
                        %mi ex
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi lex
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSet_{ex/lex}
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SEAR+plus+epsilon"} SEAR+ε
            for an application of this idea.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              CoSHEP as a choice principle added to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ZF"} ZF
              implies a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+class"} proper class
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+cardinals"} regular cardinals
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Since CoSHEP implies
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WISC"} WISC
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Benno+van+den+Berg"} van den Berg
          %h2#in_higher_category_theory  In higher category theory
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                For every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-groupoid"} 0-groupoid
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+epimorphism"} effective epimorphism
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                        %mo →
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to A
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                there exists effective epimorphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to P
                with
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            %li
              %p
                For every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-groupoid"} infinity-groupoid
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+epimorphism"} effective epimorphism
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                        %mo →
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to A
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                there exists effective epimorphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to P
                with
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
          %p
            The difference between these versions of CoSHEP is that
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets+cover"} sets cover
          %h2#justification Justification
          %p
            Although perhaps not well known in the literature of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+countable+choice"} axioms of countable choice
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+dependent+choice"} dependent choice
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ImpliesDependentAndCountableChoice"}
            above.
          %p
            To be explicit, every set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            should have a ‘completely presented’ set of ‘canonical’
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elements"} elements
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality+relation"} equality relation
            imposed upon them. For canonical elements,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"} equality
            is identity, so the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BHK+interpretation"} BHK interpretation
            of logic justifies the axiom of choice for a completely presented set. This set is
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is obtained from it as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+set"} quotient
            by the relation of equality on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+object"}> projective object
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+presentation"} projective presentation
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+cover"} projective cover
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+resolution"} projective resolution
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+module"} projective module
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internally+projective+object"} internally projective object
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+object"}> injective object
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+presentation"} injective presentation
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+envelope"} injective envelope
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+resolution"} injective resolution
              %ul
                %li
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+module"} injective module
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+object"}> free object
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+resolution"} free resolution
              %ul
                %li
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+module"} free module
            %li
              %p
                flat object,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+resolution"} flat resolution
              %ul
                %li
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+module"} flat module
          %h2#references References
          %p
            When
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Aczel"} Peter Aczel
            was developing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CZF
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CZF
            (a constructive predicative version of
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ZFC"} ZFC
            = succeed "," do
              %em presentation axiom
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Aczel"}> Peter Aczel
              ,
              = succeed "." do
                %em The type theoretic interpretation of constructive set theory
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0049-237X%2808%2971989-X"} 10.1016/S0049-237X(08)71989-X
          %p
            The presentation axiom was, however, adopted by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Erik+Palmgren"} Erik Palmgren
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CETCS
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CETCS
            (a constructive predicative version of
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ETCS"} ETCS
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Erik+Palmgren"}> Erik Palmgren
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Constructivist and Structuralist Foundations: Bishop’s and Lawvere’s Theories of Sets
              %p
                %strong 163
                Issue 10 (2012) 1384–1399, doi:
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.apal.2012.01.011"} 10.1016/j.apal.2012.01.011
                arXiv:
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1201.6272"}> 1201.6272
                ,
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.uu.se/~palmgren/cetcs.pdf"} author pdf
          %p Its relationship to some other weak axioms of choice is studied in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Rathjen"}> Michael Rathjen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Choice principles in constructive and classical set theories
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/9781316755723.014"} 10.1017/9781316755723.014
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://www1.maths.leeds.ac.uk/~rathjen/acend.pdf"} author pdf
          .property
